eck.gl/proposals/layers` renders aligned, batched, caller-owned GPUVectors."," 2. This package resolves Arrow columns, uploads adapter-owned GPUVectors, and releases them when the"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/api-reference/proposals/gpu-layers.md","lines":["@@ -10,8 +10,7 @@ The GPU layer family defines the rendering ABI below Arrow, classic JavaScript,"," inputs. It consumes caller-owned GPU data, does not import Apache Arrow, and never destroys input"," vectors."," ","-The fixed-width primitives are `GPUArcLayer`, `GPUColumnLayer`, `GPUGridCellLayer`, `GPUIconLayer`,","-`GPULineLayer`, `GPUPointCloudLayer`, and `GPUScatterplotLayer`. They consume row-aligned","+The fixed-width primitives are `GPUIconLayer` and `GPUScatterplotLayer`. They consume row-aligned"," `GPUVector` objects. Each layer owns one `GPUVectorModel`, which preserves every physical chunk as"," a separate draw call without creating a model or deck child layer per chunk. `GPUBitmapLayer`"," accepts an already loaded `Texture`; a bitmap has no tabular column to convert."],"additions":1,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/developer-guide/using-with-arrow.md","lines":["@@ -134,6 +134,8 @@ Some layers expose optional props for caller-owned luma.gl `GPUVector` buffers."," These unstable props follow the layer's GPU layout and can change at any time."," Check the layer reference for supported formats and the meaning and order of rows."," ","+Arc, Line, Column, and GridCell can bind caller-owned packed `float32x2` position vectors directly. Vertex fetch supplies zero elevation. Arc and Line accept XY and XYZ independently for each endpoint.","+"," Instanced rendering layers take values in rendered instance order. Supplied"," vectors must agree on row count and chunk boundaries. For GPU positions, choose a coordinate system that the rendering path can"," use directly. Layers that require CPU preprojection for the supplied"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated"